1. She owns a dog who is very attached to her and enjoys helping in the kitchen, especially with knives. (Verbatim: "she insisted on helping mostly because she really really likes my knives like she loves my knives she was like no no let me do it I want to I want to use the knives")

2. She is proud of her cooking skills, particularly her roast potatoes, which she describes as crunchy on the outside and fluffy on the inside. (Verbatim: "I am very proud of the roast potatoes I made. They were super super crunchy on the outside and fluffy on the inside.")

3. She cooked a traditional British Christmas dinner, including Yorkshire puddings, roast potatoes, turkey, broccoli, carrots, parsnips, sprouts, and cauliflower cheese. (Verbatim: "I cooked... Yorkshire puddings, roast potatoes... broccoli, carrots... turkey with some cranberry and some cauliflower cheese.")

4. She owns a high-quality Japanese knife that she loves and brought from Japan. (Verbatim: "I got a very fancy a very fancy Japanese knife all the way from Japan and yeah I love that knife.")

5. She refers to family members as "mama elia," "papa elia," "little ellie bro," and "older ellie bro," suggesting a close but possibly complex family dynamic. (Verbatim: "mama elia and um little ellie bro come around... papa elia and my older ellie bro turned up")

6. Her younger brother had not spoken to her father for years, but they reconnected during Christmas, which she helped facilitate. (Verbatim: "little elie bro and my father spoke for like the first time in years... it was awkward... I was like heck to the no you are not [leaving]")

7. She dislikes playing Monopoly, especially in family settings, because she believes it causes conflict. (Verbatim: "I was like please no... I'm trying to connect the family not trying to break it... monopoly... capitalism and breaking up families let's go")

8. She played Mario-themed board games during the holidays, including "Blow Up Shaky Towers," which involves balancing characters on a tower. (Verbatim: "we played... Blow Up Shaky Towers... you place the characters on it to like balance it out and then whoever makes the ball drop loses")

9. She wears Christmas-themed attire and plans to keep it on until the 12 days of Christmas have passed. (Verbatim: "I'm still in my christmas gear... up until the 12 days of christmas then i will change back into regular gear")

10. She enjoys role-playing while cooking, such as wearing an apron and getting into the "role of chef." (Verbatim: "i like to get into the role of chef") [end of text]



1. She is British. (Verbatim: "yeah like i'm british i can't even do that there's a lot of british people out there")
