1. She had a difficult childhood kitchen environment with broken appliances and a complicated gas stove system. (Verbatim: "we had a very specific method to use the stove at my parents... the ignition like thingy didn't actually work so you had to get like a separate tool to get that running")

2. She felt excited and amazed when she first experienced a fully functional kitchen after moving out for university. (Verbatim: "when i first moved out i discovered that people have kitchens with that actually have functioning things inside i was amazed by an oven that could work")

3. Her family had planned to renovate their kitchen, which was designed and saved for, but the renovation was ultimately cancelled. (Verbatim: "we were supposed to have the kitchen fixed... it was very very very exciting and then that got cancelled yeah because because of things")

4. She currently has a modern and functional kitchen that she considers "fancy," despite having a microwave from a bin. (Verbatim: "my kitchen's good now it's so good... it's a fancy kitchen even if some people may not say it's fancy just because the microwave is from the bin")

5. She prefers gas stoves with open flames over flat electric hobs, missing the visual and sensory experience of fire while cooking. (Verbatim: "i find that very odd i miss the flames i miss being able to use like um a wok... where's the heat where's the fire")

6. She aspires to be financially responsible and fulfill her dream of creating the kitchen she once envisioned. (Verbatim: "one day i'll make that kitchen come true one day... just yeah be financially responsible")

7. She struggled with loneliness and felt like an outcast during her school years, describing herself as "the weird girl" that nobody wanted to hang out with. (Verbatim: "nobody wanted to hang out with the weird girl... that was me for a very long time")

8. She finds it hard not to feel like she’s not doing enough, indicating ongoing self-doubt despite her success. (Verbatim: "it's so hard to not think that i'm not doing enough")

9. She believes kindness is lacking in the world and makes a conscious effort to be kind because she doesn’t know what others are going through. (Verbatim: "i always want to try my best is to be kind just just because i don't know what's going on with y'all")

10. She finds meaning in knowing people now want to spend time with her, contrasting her current community with her isolated past. (Verbatim: "the fact that so many people want to spend time with me now is just like something i'd never been able to convince myself back then could happen") [end of text]



